# Source comments

Every TypeScript file we write starts with a short file comment. One to three lines. It says what the file is for.

Every function and method has a short comment on the line above it. One or two lines. It says what that function does.

Skip generated files under `client/components/ui`, dependencies, and config that has no functions. Tests get a file comment. The `it` description is the case comment.

Write the way you would tell a teammate who has not opened this file. Use everyday words. When a name is specialist language, say what it means in that file's opening comment. A cue, for example, is one subtitle. Do not restate the function name.
